===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To apply paint to.
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=I|passage=The half-dozen pieces {{...}} were '''painted''' white and carved with festoons of flowers, birds and cupids. To display them the walls had been tinted a vivid blue which had now faded, but the carpet, which had evidently been stored and recently relaid, retained its original turquoise.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To apply in the manner that paint is applied.
# {{lb|en|transitive|medicine}} To apply with a brush in order to treat some body part.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cover (something) with spots of colour, like paint.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King John|act=IV|scene=ii|passage=not '''painted''' with the crimson spots of blood}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Love's Labour's Lost|passage=Cuckoo buds of yellow hue / Do '''paint''' the meadows with delight.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To create (an image) with paints.
#: {{ux|en|to '''paint''' a portrait or a landscape}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To practise the art of painting pictures.
#: {{ux|en|I've been '''painting''' since I was a young child.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|GUI}} To [[draw]] an element in a [[graphical user interface]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=Ernest R Tello|title=Object-oriented Programming for Windows| passage=Sent to a minimized window when the icon's background must be filled before it is '''painted'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figuratively}} To [[depict]] or [[portray]].
#: {{ux|en|She sued the author of the biography, claiming it '''painted''' her as a duplicitous fraud.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Much Ado About Nothing|act=III|scene=ii|passage=Disloyal? / The word is too good to '''paint''' out her wickedness.}}
#* {{RQ:Pope Works|volume=II|title=Epistle 2|lines=15–16|page=62|passage=VVhether the Charmer ſinner it, or ſaint it, / VVhen Folly grovvs romantic, vve muſt '''paint''' it.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-GB|author=Victoria Bekiempis|title=FTX co-founder testifies he committed crimes with Sam Bankman-Fried|work=The Guardian|date=2023-10-05|url=https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/oct/05/sam-bankman-fried-ftx-adam-yedidia|issn=0261-3077|passage= During defense openings, Bankman-Fried’s lawyer '''painted''' him as a “nerd” who tried to do the right thing but was overwhelmed with a fast-growing company.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To color one's face by way of beautifying it.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Hamlet|act=V|scene=i|passage=Let her '''paint''' an inch thick.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|military|slang}} To direct a [[radar]] [[beam]] toward.
#:{{usex|en|"We'll '''paint''' the target for the flyboys," the JTAC said.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2023|author=J. Allen Hynek|title=The UFO Experience: Evidence Behind Close Encounters, Project Blue Book, and the Search for Answers|publisher=Red Wheel/Weiser|isbn=9781633412903|page=73|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ftWHEAAAQBAJ&pg=PA73&dq=%22painted%22+radar&hl=&cd=14&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22painted%22%20radar&f=false|text=The Albuquerque radar “'''painted'''” just one object whenever the light was on, none when it was off.}}

